# This repository tracks the Lewis Hamilton site only.
#
# Deny-by-default, then allow the site's own files. Everything else in this
# working directory — the reference material it was studied against
# (reference/), the planning docs, the tooling used to produce them — stays
# local. That also covers node_modules/, dist/, .vite/, logs and the
# full-resolution exports in asset-sources/: none of them is allowed below.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/index.html
!/on-track.html
!/off-track.html
!/calendar.html
!/partials/
!/public/
!/src/
!/tools/
!/media/
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/tsconfig.json
!/vite.config.ts
!/vercel.json

# NOTE: there was an ignore rule here for public/assets/helmet/helmet.glb,
# added when the reference site's own helmet briefly sat at that filename. That
# model is gone, and our own packed helmet now lives at exactly that path — so
# the rule was silently untracking the asset the hero needs to render. Removed
# deliberately; do not reinstate it by filename. If a third-party model ever
# needs excluding again, give it a name that ours cannot collide with.

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
